export anchor WarmMinimalStyle:
    number: 189
    screen: ProjectsDashboard
    name: Warm minimal
    idea: A calm, paper-like workspace in cream and warm brown, where one terracotta accent marks what to act on, corners are a soft 6px and a humanist sans keeps the tone friendly and unhurried.
    base: light
    palette:
        cream: #f7f1e6, the page and the top bar
        paper: #fffbf4, panels, fields and the style sheet
        ink: #2b2420, headings and body text
        bark: #665548, meta, labels and axis text
        sand: #e4d8c6, 1px lines and the progress track, never text
        terracotta: #a8492a, the primary button, current nav text, this week's line, links and focus
        clay: #f5e3d6, the tint behind the current nav, the overdue figure and avatars
        moss: #2f6a3e, On track with a line circle and check
        ochre: #855300, At risk with a line triangle and bar
        brick: #962a2a, Behind and the overdue figure, with a line square and cross
    type:
        One humanist stack, Seravek, Gill Sans Nova, Ubuntu, Calibri,
        Optima, Candara, DejaVu Sans, sans-serif, in weights 400 and 600.
        The greeting is 34px semibold, KPI figures 30px semibold tabular,
        section titles 19px semibold, body 15px at 1.55, and meta, labels
        and chips 13px.
    layout:
        A cream top bar edged by one sand line holds a terracotta square
        mark with the brand, six text nav links with Home in a clay pill,
        and at right a search field, a terracotta New project button, a
        bell button and the initials disc with Mara Okafor. Content sits
        in a centred 1120px column. The hero row puts the greeting, date
        and an overdue line with a square symbol and a Review them link at
        left, and at right one paper strip split by thin rules into four
        figures with a small icon and label, the overdue cell tinted clay
        with a brick figure. Below, two columns at 7 to 5. The left panel
        lists the six projects as rows with name, team, due date and days
        left, then a 6px bar with percent and tasks, then the status word
        with its line symbol. The right column stacks a line chart panel,
        this week as a solid terracotta line over a faint area with value
        labels and last week as a dashed bark line with square markers,
        totals beneath, and an activity panel with clay initial discs and
        times under each line. Below 1040px everything stacks and the
        search fills the bar. On phones the nav wraps under the brand,
        the New project button shows only its plus, the figures form a 2
        by 2 grid and project bars drop under the name.
    spacing: An 8px unit. 24px panel padding, 32px between sections and columns, 16px row padding.
    density: Comfortable. Six project rows and six activity items without crowding.
    corners: 6px on panels, buttons, fields, the progress bar and nav pills. Avatars are round.
    borders: 1px sand lines around panels and between rows and figures.
    shadows: One soft warm shadow, 0 1px 2px at 6 percent brown, on panels only.
    icons: Thin 1.6px line icons at 15 to 18px in bark. Status symbols are line shapes in the status colour, a circle with a check, a triangle with a bar and a square with a cross.
    focus: A 2px terracotta outline offset 2px. A focused field also takes a clay fill.
    tone: Warm and plain in sentence case, such as Welcome back, Mara and 4 tasks are overdue.
